.TH GHOSTLIGHT 1 "2026-10-20" "Ghostlight 2.0.1" "Ghostlight Manual"
.SH NAME
ghostlight \- governed browser automation for MCP clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghostlight
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ghostlight gives an MCP client controlled access to your own visible Chromium
browser. It runs entirely on this computer: there is no account, no telemetry,
and no hosted service.
.PP
Run with no command, it opens the desktop workbench. Nothing runs in the
background until an agent or your browser asks for it.
.PP
.B ghostlight
is a small program that does three jobs. It is the stdio server an MCP client
launches (as
.BR "ghostlight mcp" ),
it is the native messaging host Chromium
starts for the Ghostlight extension, and it hands every other command to the
service program,
.BR ghostlight\-service ,
installed beside it. The service program holds all product decisions and state.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mcp
Run as a local stdio MCP server. An MCP client starts it with this argument,
and
.B install
registers it in each client's configuration. It is not meant to be run by hand.
.TP
.B open
Open the desktop workbench, starting the local authority if it is not running.
.TP
.BR install " [" \-\-dry\-run "] [" \-\-browser " \fIid\fR] [" \-\-all\-browsers "] [" \-\-client " \fIid\fR] [" \-\-all\-clients "] [" \-\-no\-clients "] [" \-\-no\-open ]
Register the browser native-messaging host and every detected MCP client.
Repeating an install changes nothing that is already current.
.B \-\-client
selects one agent by its id, with each of its hosts that is detected, or one
host by its host id, ignoring case; repeat it to select more. With
.B \-\-all\-clients
an agent id selects every host of the agent, detected or not.
.br
Agent ids: codex, claude\-code, claude\-desktop, cursor, vscode, windsurf, devin, zed, zcode, opencode, crush, copilot\-cli, cline, kiro, qwen\-code, junie, kilo\-code, goose, continue, antigravity
.br
Host ids: cline\-cli, cline\-vscode, cline\-cursor, cline\-windsurf
.TP
.BR uninstall " [" \-\-dry\-run "] [" \-\-browser " \fIid\fR] [" \-\-client " \fIid\fR]"
Remove only Ghostlight-owned registrations and stop the running Ghostlight.
Foreign configuration is preserved byte for byte, and
.I ~/.ghostlight
stays. It ends by saying what it removed and what it kept;
.B \-\-dry\-run
lists what it would remove.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-fix ]
Report the complete local chain: environment, installed programs, browser
registrations, the command entry, the Applications entry, MCP clients, and the
service endpoint.
.B \-\-fix
applies only ownership-safe repairs.
.B \-\-json
prints the same observation as one JSON document and cannot be combined with
.BR \-\-fix .
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
Report the local service endpoint without starting it.
.TP
.BI call " tool" " [json]"
Run one browser tool and print its outcome.
.B \-\-stdin
runs a batch over one session,
.B \-\-json
prints the structured result, and
.BI \-\-output " file"
writes bounded binary content such as a screenshot.
.B \-\-catalog
lists the available tools, and
.B \-\-help
prints the usage, the exit codes and the scripting guide's path.
.TP
.BR diagnostics " path|show|prune|on|off"
Read the shared process diagnostics log, or turn it on and off.
.B path
prints the log directory,
.B show
prints recent entries (with
.BR \-\-last ,
.BR \-\-component ,
.B \-\-op
and
.BR \-\-json ),
and
.B prune
removes old logs.
.TP
.BI "policy validate" " file"
Validate one schema-4 policy document.
.TP
.BI "policy migrate" " file"
Move a schema-3 policy document to schema 4. The command keeps a copy as
.IB file .schema3.bak
and refuses, leaving the file as it is, when moving it would change what the policy does.
.TP
.BI "policy explain" " file"
Explain a policy and the RAWX capability map in plain language.
.TP
.BI "policy simulate" " file audit.jsonl"
Preview denials against existing audit records without changing anything.
.TP
.BI "policy keygen" " directory"
Create customer-owned policy signing keys.
.TP
.B policy pubkey
Print the public bootstrap verification keys.
.TP
.B policy sign
Sign a policy document at an explicit sequence.
.TP
.B policy publish
Advance the sequence and prepare a deployment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B ghostlight call
maps the terminal outcome to a distinct status. An uncertain effect is never
reported as success.
.TP
.B 0
The work succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
The command line could not be understood.
.TP
.B 2
Authority blocked the work.
.TP
.B 4
The work failed.
.TP
.B 5
The work was cancelled.
.TP
.B 6
The effect is unknown. Do not assume it did or did not happen.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GHOSTLIGHT_SESSION
Pin a command-line session explicitly. It is a caller's claim, never an input
to an authority decision.
.TP
.B GHOSTLIGHT_POLICY_FILE
Use an exact local policy document. It takes precedence over the workbench's
authored user policy, which is then shown read-only.
.TP
.B GHOSTLIGHT_AUDIT_FILE
Write audit records to an exact path.
.TP
.B GHOSTLIGHT_DIAGNOSTICS_DIR
Turn process diagnostics on and write them to an exact directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ghostlight/bin
The installed programs,
.BR ghostlight ,
.B ghostlight\-service
and
.BR ghostlight\-desktop ,
and
.IR install.json ,
the record of what the install put there.
.TP
.I ~/.ghostlight/policy
The authored user policy.
.TP
.I ~/.ghostlight/state
Local state, including the append-only audit record
.IR audit.jsonl .
.TP
.I ~/.ghostlight/diagnostics
Process diagnostics logs, written only while diagnostics are on.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/ghostlight
The command entry the installation owns, a link to
.IR ~/.ghostlight/bin/ghostlight .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/org.sylin.ghostlight.desktop
The Applications entry the installation owns.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1/ghostlight.1
This manual page.
.B man
finds it because it searches
.I ../share/man
for every directory on PATH.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/ghostlight
.TQ
.I ~/.local/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/ghostlight.fish
Shell completions the installation owns. Both shells read these
locations without configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions/_ghostlight
The zsh completion. Zsh does not read this directory by default. To use it,
add this line to your
.I .zshrc
before
.BR compinit :
.B fpath+=(~/.local/share/zsh/site-functions)
.PP
.B ghostlight uninstall
removes the entries under
.I ~/.local
and keeps
.IR ~/.ghostlight .
Deleting that folder removes the programs, the audit history and the settings.
.SH NOTES
Snap and Flatpak browser packages cannot start a native messaging host, so they
are detected and refused with a remedy rather than failing silently. Install a
native Chrome, Edge, Brave, or Chromium package.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://sylin.org/ghostlight/
